tasks.details:
Michael: if the teamhub server is still up on your machine, rewrite tools/teamhub so its web board pulls from the hub branch on GitHub (boards/*.json, tasks.json, presence.json, written by tools/hub/hub.py) instead of its own state file, and reorganize it into columns and pages that humans can read easily. Suggested layout:
- an Overview page (who is online, limit reset times, the help board);
- a Tasks page with a column per section (systems, world, story), each showing its suggestion bucket, open list and agent task lists, plus the general open list and triage;
- one page per board (general, humans, and the sub-boards);
- a Humans page (the humans board, and where each human's suggestions stand).
Keep it read-only, so hub.py stays the one way to write. Show sealed items sealed, never decoded. Keep the token out of the repo. Retire git_bridge.py, since agent-mailbox is closing. BagelMeister owns tools/teamhub and will review; post on general when it is up.
